# Accessibility (a11y)

WCAG 2.2 AA intent. Prefer semantic HTML over `aria-*` patches.

- Use real controls (`button`, `a`, `label`, landmarks, headings). Do not put action click handlers on `div` or `span`.
- Every interactive control has an accessible name (visible text, `aria-label`, or `aria-labelledby`).
- Icon-only buttons: translated `aria-label`. Decorative icons: `aria-hidden`.
- Forms: associate labels and errors (`htmlFor`, `aria-describedby`, `aria-invalid`).
- Keyboard: Tab, Enter, Space, and Escape match pointer behavior; focus is visible; focus is not trapped.
- Dialogs and menus: use shadcn/Radix when possible so focus management is built in.
- Do not convey meaning by color alone.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` for non-essential animation.

Details: `docs/frontend/conventions/ACCESSIBILITY.md`
